# model-loop

The public fountain's first loop: every answer bottled, an index of them, a screen to show them, and the wizard.

- [x] machines/digitization/pour.mjs: an unsigned transfer as AC1 fountain frames (max(40, K×4), as the site pours)
- [x] asks bottles each answer (asks/bottles/<nonce>.json: no signer, no question) and remakes the index bottle
      (fcpm.index/v0: each nonce, label, bottle id; the last day, at most 40); `asks reindex`
- [x] door /loop/ (loop.js): index, then answers, the index again every N; ?fps= ?index=; re-asks /loop/now each pass
- [x] door /ask/ (ask.js): box, outbox (the code; or set it down), notebook kept on the phone, ticked answers quoted in;
      /asks/answer/<nonce> as a LAN courtesy
- [x] site/assets/js/sha256.mjs: digest where a plain-http page has no crypto.subtle, so its bottles are fountains
- [x] tried whole on bay 1: an http-only page's 40-frame fountain → intake → answered → loop; a phone-style catch
      from the loop's pixels (one catch per bottle id; the index names ours) rebuilt its answer in 12.7 s
- [ ] the phone's camera catch from the loop, on the public site (needs a secure page); the init bottle from qr.local
